{"id": "EUVD-2026-102362", "enisaUuid": "0cf99b1e-93a0-3c41-8b20-381803379f73", "description": "libxmp through 4.7.4 contains an off-by-one stack out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the prowizard P61A depacker depack_p61a() in src/loaders/prowizard/p61a.c. Attackers can supply a crafted headerless P61A module with 31 samples and a 0xffe0 back-reference size word to leak stack memory into sample metadata or disrupt loading.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:50:44", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libxmp-p61a-sample-backreference-oob-read", "https://github.com/libxmp/libxmp/blob/5d4f6aa2c7dcdf8e9cd8129fe579d45b36a302da/src/loaders/prowizard/p61a.c#L110-L116", "https://github.com/libxmp/libxmp/blob/5d4f6aa2c7dcdf8e9cd8129fe579d45b36a302da/src/loaders/prowizard/p61a.c#L638-L641", "https://github.com/libxmp/libxmp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libxmp-through-4.7.4-stack-out-of-bounds-read-via-p61a-depacker"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111131", "GHSA-5xv9-8cq8-34q7"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c1f65e6f-340f-30b0-884a-f1c911d0d637", "product": {"name": "Libxmp", "vendor": {"name": "Libxmp"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.7.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4d851cb2-6833-3757-8672-99817f497d6c", "vendor": {"name": "Libxmp"}}], "isExploited": false}